    "wiki_index_first": true,
    "wiki_index_hits": 24,
    "synthesis_max_output_tokens": 8192,
    "inference_label": "【推論】",
    "answer_guidance": "Use the user's language. Cite curated Wiki pages first; cite Raw only where the Wiki lacks the claim. Separate market demand, technical measurement need and R&S product/options; for an open-ended product question cover distinct instrument roles. For a product/market mapping or recommendation question, write a report: a one-line 建議主軸; then '### 推薦先賣' with a few cited lines, or 知識庫未證實 when no passage ties a product to that market; then '### 產品與 Option 對接表' as a Markdown table with columns 產品線 | 可接軌的需求 | 知識庫確認的 option / 規格 | 為什麼適合 | 證據 | 缺口 / 報價風險, one row per product line, citing its passages in the 證據 cell; then '### 場景切入建議' as a table 場景 | 推薦組合 | 切入重點 | 未驗證事項, each row cited; then '### 限制'. For other questions lead with a short answer, then cited details. List only option codes and specifications that appear in the passages; write 知識庫未標示 instead of guessing a code, order number, price, market share or competitor advantage. A press release's positioning is not measured demand, and a target-market list is not customer fit. Put any conclusion that connects separate sources on a labeled inference line. Claim that a product fits a market, application or customer only where a cited passage states that link; otherwise give the product facts and write 知識庫未證實 for the link. Do not rank (strongest, most important) unless a passage ranks. A table cell or heading must not state a link the passages do not state. These instructions are not knowledge: never repeat their evidence rules or facet names (such as direct_relationship) as findings, and never cite a passage for them. Answer every part of the question: for each part, state each cited fact the passages give for it rather than only the first few; a longer answer is fine when every line is cited.",
    "citation_policy": "wiki_primary",
    "bilingual_retrieval": true,
    "retrieval_rounds": 2,
    "evidence_sections": 96,
    "evidence_chars": 80000,
    "evidence_sections_per_page": 8
  }
}
